  "title": "New Imperialism (colonial expansion of the late 1800s)",
  "summary": "In the late 1800s industrialized European nations moved quickly to seize Africa for raw materials, new markets, prestige and military dominance, and the United States, Germany and Japan also sought overseas colonies. The Scramble for Africa peaked at the Berlin Conference of 1884–1885, where Europeans allotted parts of the continent to one another without African input. Colonization continued through the 1880s to the 1910s.",
